  "candidate_policy": "Only explicit zero-passability code or exact total-blockage descriptions, or an explicit user override, can identify a future-cut candidate. Unknown passability never establishes complete blockage. The location must be within 50 m, have a unique positively identified own-stream channel, and be clear of junction ambiguity. No cuts are applied.",
  "identity_policy": "Search every physical channel within 50 m; compare its local course using multiple samples and headings against named hydrography with LLIDs, independent of fish distribution. Require a unique own-stream channel and unambiguous reference-route support. Unknown, unnamed, conflicting, competing-channel, or junction-ambiguous matches remain for manual review. Numbered location-review points are not necessarily approved stream assignments.",
